  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">From Vulnerability to Resilience, Climate Adapted Livelihoods for Vulnerable Communities in Bihar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed project titled &quot;From Vulnerability to Resilience, Climate Adapted Livelihoods for Vulnerable Communities in Bihar&quot; aims to build a climate-resilient rural economy in two of Bihar&#x2019;s most climate-vulnerable blocks: Raniganj (Araria) and K-Nagar (Purnea)&#x2014;where marginalized communities such as women, Scheduled Castes/Tribes, Muslims, and persons with disabilities face entrenched poverty, exclusion, and fragile livelihoods. Located in the flood-prone Kosi-Seemanchal belt, these areas are highly exposed to recurrent floods, erratic monsoons, and drought-like conditions. High dependence on rainfed agriculture, predominance of small and marginal landholders, and weak health and institutional systems further exacerbate their vulnerability. Against this backdrop, the project integrates climate-smart agriculture, livelihood diversification, disaster preparedness, and convergence with government schemes to reduce risks, secure livelihoods, and empower the most disadvantaged&#x2014;with a strong emphasis on women farmers as key agents of change.</narrative>
  </description>
